@* Under the box an outreach template is written in (Outreach templates): what happens to its placeholders, and the
   ways to say what happens when one has nothing to fill. Every placeholder, with what it becomes, is in the Insert
   menu (OutreachInsertMenu), and whether TIDE can fill the draft is the check line above this. *@
<div class="form-text" id="@Id">
    Filled from the action when the email is written. Parts above the TLP ceiling are left out, and anything with
    nothing to fill is marked for you to fix before sending.
</div>
<details class="tide-outreach-help small mt-1">
    <summary>When there's nothing to fill</summary>
    <dl class="tide-outreach-placeholders mt-2">
        <dt class="tide-data">{{article.other-links?}}</dt>
        <dd>Dropped, with its line when it's alone on it.</dd>
        <dt class="tide-data">{{product.contact|there}}</dt>
        <dd>"there" is written instead.</dd>
        <dt class="tide-data">{{#article.cves}} … {{else}} … {{/article.cves}}</dt>
        <dd>What's before {{else}} when there's something to fill, what's after it when there isn't. Without {{else}},
            the whole section goes, heading and all.</dd>
    </dl>
</details>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Id { get; set; } = "";
}
